    "claim": "Pulmonary arterial hypertension and gynecomastia are postulated to result from the inhibition of SRC family kinases and other associated pathways.",
    "verdict": "SUPPORTED",
    "rationale": "The first abstract attributes pulmonary arterial hypertension to 'Src kinase inhibition', and the third abstract postulates that gynecomastia results from 'inhibition of various kinases, including src family kinases and receptor kinases'."
  },
